---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout active="home">
  <div class="body" style="max-width: 920px">
    <p class="eyebrow">Overview</p>
    <h1>Mru documentation</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="max-width: 40ch">
      Reference for Mru&#39;s open core, for unattended missions with no repair path: the shrinking-quorum runtime, the
      Dusk simulator, and the tools around them.
    </p>

    <h2>Where to start</h2>
    <div class="cards two" style="margin-top: 8px">
      <a class="card" href="/concepts/shrinking-quorum/#degradation-first" style="text-decoration: none">
        <p class="k">Concepts</p>
        <h3 class="h3">Degradation-first design</h3>
        <p class="small soft" style="margin: 10px 0 0">
          The Degradation-First Principle and the shrinking quorum that applies it: what is proved, what is tested, and
          what it costs.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="/core/quorum-crate/" style="text-decoration: none">
        <p class="k">Core runtime</p>
        <h3 class="h3">
          The <code>quorum</code> crate
        </h3>
        <p class="small soft" style="margin: 10px 0 0">
          Vote on three, compare on two, self-check on one. <code>no_std</code>, no allocation, checked with Kani.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="/simulation/dusk/" style="text-decoration: none">
        <p class="k">Simulation</p>
        <h3 class="h3">Dusk</h3>
        <p class="small soft" style="margin: 10px 0 0">
          A Monte Carlo of redundancy policies on hardware that only ever decays. 10,000 missions in about two seconds.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="/core/fprime/" style="text-decoration: none">
        <p class="k">Integrations</p>
        <h3 class="h3">F&#180; and OPS-SAT</h3>
        <p class="small soft" style="margin: 10px 0 0">
          F&#180; components around the Rust core, a C interface for other frameworks, and the operations note for a
          proposed OPS-SAT experiment.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="/lab/2049/" style="text-decoration: none">
        <p class="k">Lab</p>
        <h3 class="h3">Mru 2049</h3>
        <p class="small soft" style="margin: 10px 0 0">
          A browser flight simulator on real astronomical data. 109,389 stars, planets correct for any date.
        </p>
      </a>
    </div>

    <h2 id="quickstart">Quickstart</h2>
    <p>You need a Rust toolchain. Clone the runtime, run its tests, then run the demo with two replicas killed.</p>
    <pre class="pre" tabindex="0"><span class="c"># the runtime and its demo</span>
git clone https://github.com/mruspace/flight
<span class="k">cd</span> flight
cargo test --workspace
cargo run --release --bin quorum -- --policy shrink --ticks 20000 --seed 1 \
  --upset-rate 0.001 --fault kill:0@5000 --fault kill:1@10000</pre>
    <p style="margin-top: 16px">
      Run the same seed with <code>--policy tmr</code> to compare. The first two lines of each run:
    </p>
    <pre class="pre" tabindex="0">policy=shrink ticks=20000 seed=1 upset_rate=0.001
<span class="s">useful=14989</span> detected=11 wrong=0 halted_at=never alive_at_end=1 stopped=completed last_useful=20000

policy=tmr ticks=20000 seed=1 upset_rate=0.001
useful=9990 detected=9 wrong=0 <span class="s">halted_at=10000</span> alive_at_end=1 stopped=halted last_useful=9999</pre>
    <p class="tiny" style="margin-top: 10px">
      flight v0.2.0 on an Apple M4. The counts depend only on the seed.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 16px">
      Fixed TMR halts at tick 10000, when the second replica dies. The shrinking quorum keeps running on the last
      replica, which checks its own work.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 16px">Then the simulator, which needs no dependencies:</p>
    <pre class="pre" tabindex="0">git clone https://github.com/mruspace/dusk
<span class="k">cd</span> dusk
cargo run --release --bin dusk              <span class="c"># 10,000 missions, about 2 s</span>
cargo run --release --bin dusk -- --sweep   <span class="c"># sensitivity, about 1 minute</span></pre>
    <p class="tiny" style="margin-top: 10px">
      Times on an Apple M4 with 10 cores.
    </p>

